[{"id":"SEC-1","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":"src/storage/store.js","line":25,"what_breaks":"The load-time shape check tests only types, never the rules the domain enforces. Hand-edited or older data loads as valid even when it has an empty customer name, a negative or non-integer-range quantity, a negative or huge unitPriceCents, a date that is not a calendar date, or an email without an @. The app then shows these values as normal and puts them in totals.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"hasValidShape (lines 25-29) calls allStrings and Number.isInteger only. The stored value {version:1,nextOrderNumber:1,customers:[{id:'c',name:'',email:'x',phone:''}],orders:[{id:'o',number:1,customerId:'c',date:'nope',lines:[{id:'l',description:'',quantity:-3,unitPriceCents:-5}]}]} passes every check, so load returns ok:true. Once loaded, formatEuros(-5) runs Math.floor(-0.05) = -1 and String(-5 % 100) = '-5', and renders '€-1.-5'. I traced this by reading the code. A node probe was refused by the scope guard, so I have not run it.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-2","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":"src/storage/store.js","line":21,"what_breaks":"Stored references are trusted without a check. An order's customerId is never checked against the customers, and ids are not checked for duplicates. An orphan order shows as 'Unknown customer' and no customer filter can find it. With duplicate order ids, updateOrderDate, deleteOrder and the line edits match every copy at once.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"isOrder only checks that customerId is a string. Nothing compares it with data.customers. orders.js deleteOrder filters by id and updateOrderDate maps by id, so two orders stored with id 'o' are both changed or both removed by one click. Probe: put an order with customerId 'ghost' in localStorage['invoice-app'], reload, and open the Orders tab.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-3","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":"src/storage/store.js","line":26,"what_breaks":"nextOrderNumber is not checked against the order numbers already stored. If hand-edited or older data has nextOrderNumber at or below an existing number, the next new order gets a duplicate number. A-04 says order numbers are never reused.","requirement":"R-07","evidence":"hasValidShape only checks Number.isInteger(data.nextOrderNumber). With nextOrderNumber:1 and an existing order number:1, addOrder (orders.js line 19) creates a second order numbered 1. I traced this by reading the code. Probe: store that state, reload, and create an order.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-4","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/app.js","line":5,"what_breaks":"window.localStorage is read at module top level, outside any try. When storage is disabled (for example the browser blocks all site data or cookies), the getter throws a SecurityError. The module never finishes loading, nothing renders under the header, and the banner never shows. The error appears only in the console. The store's own catch around getItem is never reached.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"Line 5: const store = createStore(window.localStorage); has no try around it. store.load wraps only storage.getItem. Manual probe: in Chrome, block all site data for localhost, reload http://localhost:8000, and check whether the banner shows an error or the page is blank.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-5","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/app.js","line":23,"what_breaks":"crypto.randomUUID only exists in secure contexts. If the app is opened from a non-localhost http address (for example a LAN IP), newId throws a TypeError inside the submit handler. Add customer, New order and Add line then do nothing, with no message on the page.","requirement":"R-01","evidence":"newId: () => crypto.randomUUID() is called before the domain call in customers-view.js line 158, orders-view.js line 123 and lines-view.js line 105, and none of these is guarded. Manual probe: serve with python3 -m http.server 8000 and open http://<LAN-IP>:8000, then add a customer.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-6","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":"src/storage/store.js","line":31,"what_breaks":"Raw exception messages are shown in the banner. A JSON.parse SyntaxError message can include part of the stored text, and DOMException messages differ by browser. Everything goes through textContent, so nothing can run as markup. This is only an exposure of internals in the page.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"readableError returns error.message. app.js showError sets banner.textContent, which is safe as text. Probe: set localStorage['invoice-app'] to '{bad' and reload to see the message text.","proven":false},{"id":"SEC-7","class":"security","severity":"advisory","file":".github/workflows/gate.yml","line":16,"what_breaks":"CI checks out ioanbitza/sdlc-kit at its default branch with no pinned ref or sha, then runs its gate.mjs. Any later change to that repository changes what CI runs and what it passes, without a change in this repository.","requirement":"none","evidence":"The step 'uses: actions/checkout@v4 with repository: ioanbitza/sdlc-kit, path: .sdlc-kit' has no 'ref:'. It is followed by 'run: node .sdlc-kit/tools/gate.mjs --strict'. Probe: check whether ADR-002 means the gate version to be fixed.","proven":false}]
